Short:        AGA graphics/Bob fixes for AMOS Pro
Author:       HWARF (Jerome)
Uploader:     amethist rumor786 passinbox com (Jerome)
Type:         dev/amos
Version:      0.14.1
Requires:     AMOS Professional, AGA chipset, 68020+
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet

Description:
  AMOSPro AGA Extension is an unofficial extension for AMOS
  Professional on AGA Amiga computers and AGA-enabled WinUAE.
  Version 0.14.1 is a stability and bug-fix update to 0.14.0.
  No new commands: 100 commands/functions, 203 AP20 entries.
  Motorola 68020/68EC020 minimum.

  Fixes in P2d-L2b:
    - Iff Load and Back Fill acquire Safe before bitmap writes.
    - First B8 Bob binding acquires an available Safe reply.
    - Screen Pattern draws on the Safe back buffer, not front,
      with bounded waiting and no implicit Swap.
    - Source provenance and regression tooling aligned.

  Validation:
    - Native Gate A: 184 Pattern cases, 172 writers, 10 Bob suites.
    - WinUAE Runtime: Pattern, Open/Close, cursor, FICON/FICHIP,
      AGBO/B8, AGPC, C2P, Copper, End and system font checks PASS.
    - Memory stable after warmup in repeated lifecycle tests.
    - Integrated Bob Runtime PASS supplied: 240 samples,
      252 successful swaps, 121 initial refusals recovered.
      Log matches historical P2d; L2b attribution contextual.
    - Compiler, strict interpreted mode and physical Amiga
      not requalified on L2b. Historical P2d B/C are separate.
      Exceptional OS failures and bank ABA are not exhaustive.

  Library:
    M19 P2d-L2b, 136708 bytes, SHA256:
    a7ed96e92b460e842772aed77ac35a303d8f663aaa456821c323109446dd19dc
    Internal ID: "$VER: AMOSPro_AGA M19 P2d-L2b".

  Installation:
    Back up the installed library and configuration.
    Install AMOSPro_AGA.Lib in APSystem, keep the existing
    extension slot, save configuration and restart AMOS.
    Import ASCII examples via Project / Merge ASCII.
  Only the five C2P commands require c2p.library v1.9:
    https://aminet.net/package/dev/misc/c2plib
  Iff To Chunky and Bob functions do not require it.

  Hardware AGA Sprites are not included in this version.
  Source and docs:
    https://github.com/anthea176/AMOSPro-AGA-Extension
  Source and technical documentation: MIT License.
  Artwork and assets: separate terms, see ASSETS_LICENSE.md.
  Developed by HWARF, with assistance from ChatGPT (OpenAI).
